WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:01.283
- From time to time.

00:00:01.283 --> 00:00:02.116
I like to get out of the studio

00:00:02.116 --> 00:00:03.190
to hang out with our guests,

00:00:03.190 --> 00:00:05.050
feel the sunshine and fresh air.

00:00:05.050 --> 00:00:07.949
We call these segments 'drive interviews'.

00:00:07.949 --> 00:00:09.611
(upbeat music)

00:00:09.611 --> 00:00:11.149
♪ Drive interview ♪

00:00:11.149 --> 00:00:14.130
(applause)

00:00:14.130 --> 00:00:14.963
All right.

00:00:14.963 --> 00:00:15.980
You'll never guess who showed up

00:00:15.980 --> 00:00:16.970
and in what car

00:00:16.970 --> 00:00:18.170
at the outdoor theater the other day.

00:00:18.170 --> 00:00:19.551
Take a look.

00:00:19.551 --> 00:00:22.682
(triumphant music)

00:00:22.682 --> 00:00:25.849
(upbeat techno music)

00:00:43.720 --> 00:00:44.740
- Hey you!

00:00:44.740 --> 00:00:46.071
- What's up?

00:00:46.071 --> 00:00:48.420
(dramatic upbeat music)

00:00:48.420 --> 00:00:49.520
- [Kelly] I love your car.

00:00:49.520 --> 00:00:50.413
- [David] I love your car.

00:00:50.413 --> 00:00:51.740
(dramatic upbeat music)

00:00:51.740 --> 00:00:53.439
- You win. You brought K.I.T.T.

00:00:53.439 --> 00:00:54.272
(laughing)

00:00:54.272 --> 00:00:55.150
This is amazing.

00:00:55.150 --> 00:00:56.140
(upbeat music)

00:00:56.140 --> 00:00:58.220
One of my first cars that I
ever got, I named K.I.T.T.

00:00:58.220 --> 00:00:59.530
It was a Cadillac XLR.

00:00:59.530 --> 00:01:00.363
It was black.

00:01:00.363 --> 00:01:02.400
It was like a true sports car

00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:04.905
and I was like, his name shall be K.I.T.T.

00:01:04.905 --> 00:01:06.420
(upbeat music)

00:01:06.420 --> 00:01:07.253
- K.I.T.T.'s amazing.

00:01:07.253 --> 00:01:09.200
You know, the most amazing
thing about K.I.T.T.

00:01:09.200 --> 00:01:12.300
is that today, K.I.T.T. is still relevant.

00:01:12.300 --> 00:01:14.980
Maybe after 36, 40 years later,

00:01:14.980 --> 00:01:19.210
everything is exactly what we came up with

00:01:19.210 --> 00:01:20.043
back in the day.

00:01:20.043 --> 00:01:21.150
It's weird.

00:01:21.150 --> 00:01:22.500
The cars talk.

00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:23.780
The cars drive themselves.

00:01:23.780 --> 00:01:25.070
They park.

00:01:25.070 --> 00:01:26.406
- [Kelly] Yeah. That's amazing!

00:01:26.406 --> 00:01:28.989
(upbeat music)

00:01:30.090 --> 00:01:31.690
- Speaking of Knight Rider, though,

00:01:31.690 --> 00:01:33.300
there were a lot of, like, stunts.

00:01:33.300 --> 00:01:35.270
Did you do any of the stunts?

00:01:35.270 --> 00:01:36.250
- Yeah. Y'all. Well I did.

00:01:36.250 --> 00:01:37.560
I got really good at driving

00:01:37.560 --> 00:01:38.620
because I wanted to,

00:01:38.620 --> 00:01:41.650
and the reverse 180 is,

00:01:41.650 --> 00:01:43.530
I could teach you that

00:01:43.530 --> 00:01:44.970
in about five minutes.

00:01:44.970 --> 00:01:46.280
We had no CGI

00:01:46.280 --> 00:01:49.010
and we did everything by
the seam of our pants.

00:01:49.010 --> 00:01:50.286
And the best part about it

00:01:50.286 --> 00:01:51.630
(laughing)

00:01:51.630 --> 00:01:53.660
was they would have 40 guys out there

00:01:53.660 --> 00:01:55.390
paid not to kill me.

00:01:55.390 --> 00:01:57.630
And they would say "Action, Knight Rider!"

00:01:57.630 --> 00:01:58.880
and I just go, 'Woo Hoo!'

00:01:59.790 --> 00:02:03.020
and I just do a WD-40 and spray the wheels

00:02:03.020 --> 00:02:05.080
and spin out, spin through it, go through.

00:02:05.080 --> 00:02:05.913
And they were all--.

00:02:05.913 --> 00:02:06.850
- You got paid for that!

00:02:06.850 --> 00:02:07.690
- Can you believe it?

00:02:07.690 --> 00:02:08.523
- [Kelly] That's amazing.

00:02:08.523 --> 00:02:09.725
- It's incredible.

00:02:09.725 --> 00:02:10.830
(light upbeat music)

00:02:10.830 --> 00:02:12.250
- Would you ever do a reboot?

00:02:12.250 --> 00:02:13.740
- There is a reboot in the making,

00:02:13.740 --> 00:02:15.400
so we'll see what happens.

00:02:15.400 --> 00:02:16.233
- Yeah.

00:02:16.233 --> 00:02:17.940
(light techno music)

00:02:17.940 --> 00:02:20.660
- Actually, I heard,
there was a Hoff auction?

00:02:20.660 --> 00:02:21.493
- Yeah. We had an auction.

00:02:21.493 --> 00:02:22.773
- Where was the Hoff auction?

00:02:22.773 --> 00:02:23.870
- You know, I went to the Hoff auction.

00:02:23.870 --> 00:02:25.360
It was like going to my funeral.

00:02:25.360 --> 00:02:27.520
It was like going to a different time,

00:02:27.520 --> 00:02:30.100
you know, it's best just
to get rid of this stuff,

00:02:30.100 --> 00:02:32.770
sell it, give the money to charity,

00:02:32.770 --> 00:02:35.970
which I gave a lot of money to
the Global Mobility Company,

00:02:35.970 --> 00:02:37.410
which makes children walk.

00:02:37.410 --> 00:02:40.020
It creates wheelchairs for them.

00:02:40.020 --> 00:02:42.624
I've still got like four
or five auctions left.

00:02:42.624 --> 00:02:43.457
(light upbeat music)

00:02:43.457 --> 00:02:46.640
- I heard that one of your
most prized possessions,

00:02:46.640 --> 00:02:47.850
involves SpongeBob?

00:02:47.850 --> 00:02:50.653
- Yeah. One of my prize
possessions in my house

00:02:50.653 --> 00:02:52.980
is a 13 and a half foot,

00:02:52.980 --> 00:02:56.070
750 pound version of David Hasselhoff.

00:02:56.070 --> 00:02:56.903
- [Kelly] What?

00:02:56.903 --> 00:02:57.820
- Going like.

00:02:57.820 --> 00:02:58.653
(camera shutters)

00:02:58.653 --> 00:02:59.610
- I feel like you just put it

00:02:59.610 --> 00:03:00.933
right as you enter your home.

00:03:00.933 --> 00:03:03.310
(laughing)

00:03:03.310 --> 00:03:04.151
- Right as people walk in.

00:03:04.151 --> 00:03:05.340
- I was thinking about
having it as a mailbox.

00:03:05.340 --> 00:03:06.173
(laughing)

00:03:06.173 --> 00:03:07.054
- [Kelly] That would be amazing.

00:03:07.054 --> 00:03:08.810
(light techno music)

00:03:08.810 --> 00:03:10.490
You have a heavy metal album coming out?

00:03:10.490 --> 00:03:11.810
- I did a heavy metal song, you know,

00:03:11.810 --> 00:03:13.070
called 'Through the Night'.

00:03:13.070 --> 00:03:14.010
- That's so cool.

00:03:14.010 --> 00:03:15.860
- You do what's in front of you.

00:03:15.860 --> 00:03:18.220
I just go with the flow Kelly.

00:03:18.220 --> 00:03:20.560
I mean, the phone didn't
ring for 10 years,

00:03:20.560 --> 00:03:21.710
now the phone's ringing.

00:03:21.710 --> 00:03:22.543
- [Kelly] Oh my gosh.

00:03:22.543 --> 00:03:23.418
That's awesome.

00:03:23.418 --> 00:03:26.585
(upbeat techno music)

00:03:27.680 --> 00:03:28.600
I just wanted to tell you

00:03:28.600 --> 00:03:30.490
I love your show and
my kids love your show

00:03:30.490 --> 00:03:32.570
and everybody loves it
because you're honest,

00:03:32.570 --> 00:03:33.810
because you tell the truth

00:03:33.810 --> 00:03:35.470
and because you're fun, you know?

00:03:35.470 --> 00:03:36.700
- Oh, thank you.

00:03:36.700 --> 00:03:37.533
Thank you.

00:03:37.533 --> 00:03:40.582
I'm too lazy to be a
liar or anything else.

00:03:40.582 --> 00:03:42.350
(laughing)

00:03:42.350 --> 00:03:43.780
I just do me.

00:03:43.780 --> 00:03:44.790
And if you like it, cool.

00:03:44.790 --> 00:03:46.130
If you don't, that's cool.

00:03:46.130 --> 00:03:46.963
- [David] Yeah.

00:03:46.963 --> 00:03:47.796
- Yeah.

00:03:47.796 --> 00:03:48.840
Well, thank you for doing the show.

00:03:48.840 --> 00:03:49.980
- You're welcome honey.

00:03:49.980 --> 00:03:51.030
God bless. Take care.

00:03:51.030 --> 00:03:51.881
- All right later, man.

00:03:51.881 --> 00:03:52.714
- [David] All right.

00:03:52.714 --> 00:03:55.744
(upbeat techno music)

00:03:55.744 --> 00:03:56.577
- [Kelly] Later!

00:03:56.577 --> 00:03:59.987
(upbeat techno music)

00:03:59.987 --> 00:04:00.820
(applause)

00:04:00.820 --> 00:04:01.653
- All right.

00:04:01.653 --> 00:04:03.520
So is it true that you have
a new project in Germany?

00:04:03.520 --> 00:04:04.353
- I do.

00:04:04.353 --> 00:04:05.390
I have a show, a series,

00:04:05.390 --> 00:04:08.610
and it's about my time
behind the Berlin wall

00:04:08.610 --> 00:04:10.750
and it's kind of like fact or fiction

00:04:10.750 --> 00:04:12.800
and we start shooting in August

00:04:12.800 --> 00:04:15.230
and it's going to be mostly in English,

00:04:15.230 --> 00:04:16.250
but a little bit of German

00:04:16.250 --> 00:04:18.150
and it's going to be really exciting.

00:04:18.150 --> 00:04:18.983
- Oh my God.

00:04:18.983 --> 00:04:19.816
It sounds amazing.

00:04:19.816 --> 00:04:21.970
The story's incredible, just in real life.

00:04:21.970 --> 00:04:23.770
So I can't imagine it being on film.

